  "screen.project_wildlife.creature_compendium.irl_info.american_red_fox.0": "The American Red Fox is a",
  "screen.project_wildlife.creature_compendium.irl_info.american_red_fox.1": "medium-sized, quadrupedal",
  "screen.project_wildlife.creature_compendium.irl_info.american_red_fox.2": "omnivorous mammal native to",
  "screen.project_wildlife.creature_compendium.irl_info.american_red_fox.3": "North America. It is a",
  "screen.project_wildlife.creature_compendium.irl_info.american_red_fox.4": "subspecies of the European",
  "screen.project_wildlife.creature_compendium.irl_info.american_red_fox.5": "Red Fox. It inhabits a wide",
  "screen.project_wildlife.creature_compendium.irl_info.american_red_fox.6": "range of habitats, from dry",
  "screen.project_wildlife.creature_compendium.irl_info.american_red_fox.7": "brushlands to snowy forests,",
  "screen.project_wildlife.creature_compendium.irl_info.american_red_fox.8": "but are more common in",
  "screen.project_wildlife.creature_compendium.irl_info.american_red_fox.9": "temperate forests and",
  "screen.project_wildlife.creature_compendium.irl_info.american_red_fox.10": "grasslands. It is a somewhat",
  "screen.project_wildlife.creature_compendium.irl_info.american_red_fox.11": "solitary animal, living",
  "screen.project_wildlife.creature_compendium.irl_info.american_red_fox.12": "either alone until mating, or",
  "screen.project_wildlife.creature_compendium.irl_info.american_red_fox.13": "in small family groups made",
  "screen.project_wildlife.creature_compendium.irl_info.american_red_fox.14": "of a leading mated pair and",
  "screen.project_wildlife.creature_compendium.irl_info.american_red_fox.15": "their offspring, and usually",
  "screen.project_wildlife.creature_compendium.irl_info.american_red_fox.16": "the female is the leader of",
  "screen.project_wildlife.creature_compendium.irl_info.american_red_fox.17": "the group.",



